# Copy to `.env` (gitignored). Both variables are OPTIONAL — no credentials go here.
# `.env` is loaded automatically from the cwd by `extension serve`,
# `extension invoke-api-extension`, and the authenticated commands (or pass
# `--env-file <path>`); a variable already set in the shell always wins.
#
# Authentication is `commercetools auth login`: the authenticated commands reuse that
# login token (a `manage_project` principal) and read the target Project key from it.
# See docs/cli.md.

# Override the Commerce Integration Layer EXTENSIONS edge. Normally unset — it is derived from
# your login Region (docs/cli.md#which-host-each-command-talks-to). Set it only to
# point somewhere that doesn't follow the production host convention: a local edge, or
# a staging zone.
# INTEGRATION_LAYER_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Local-only config for `extension serve`, which has no Commerce Integration Layer to
# read `ctx.config` from: each `EXTENSION_CONFIG_<KEY>` is exposed to your resolvers and
# handlers as `ctx.config.<KEY>`. `serve` hot-reloads this file — edit a value and save,
# and the next request sees it with no restart.
# EXTENSION_CONFIG_BLOCKED_SKU=BLOCKED-SKU
